course: dictionary
lesson: 7600
title: A word for a prince's land
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show their meaning in their parts. Princedom starts with prince, and ends with -dom, as in kingdom. A kingdom is a land ruled by a king, so a princedom is a land ruled by a prince.
explain: «After Yaroslav died, his sons and grandsons fought each other and Rus broke into rival princedoms.» The fighting tells you the princedoms were separate lands, each with its own prince. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Rus broke into rival lands ruled by princes." It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «In 1337 the Ottomans were only a small beylik, a little Turkish princedom.» The word little tells you a princedom can be small. Princedom is an old-fashioned word, so you will mostly meet it in history books and fairy tales.
fact: Princedom means a country or land ruled by a prince.
fact: Princedom can also mean the rank or position of a prince.
fact: A principality is a close synonym: Monaco and Liechtenstein are principalities today.
fact: Wales is often called a principality.
fact: «Princedom» is a rare, old-fashioned word. Stories use it for small kingdoms ruled by princes.
exercise: «After Yaroslav died, his sons and grandsons fought each other and Rus broke into rival princedoms.» What is a princedom? | *A land ruled by a prince | A kind of castle wall | A feast held for the king's birthday | A type of small boat
exercise: Which word is the closest synonym for princedom? | Ancient | *Principality | Barely | Curt
exercise: «In 1337 the Ottomans were only a small beylik, a little Turkish princedom.» What does the word little tell you about this princedom? | It was made of gold | It had no name | It was very large and famous | *It was small
test: «After Yaroslav died, his sons and grandsons fought each other and Rus broke into rival princedoms.» Why do these princedoms not sound peaceful? | They had no princes at all | They had sailed far away across the sea | *Their princes fought each other | They were all ruled by a queen
test: Which is the best meaning of princedom? | A type of royal jewel | *A land ruled by a prince, or a prince's rank | A ship that carries kings | A dance held in a palace
exam: After reading, which explains what princedom means best? | A tall tower built by the Mongols | *A land ruled by a prince, or the rank of a prince | A large book about the history of kings | A group of soldiers guarding a castle gate
